1
00:00:00,950 --> 00:00:04,880
Every year, pests destroy up to 40% of the world's crops.

2
00:00:04,930 --> 00:00:08,240
And as the climate warms, many of them breed faster.

3
00:00:08,290 --> 00:00:10,240
So farmers spray more often,

4
00:00:10,290 --> 00:00:13,450
pay more, and their soil grows poorer.

5
00:00:13,950 --> 00:00:16,540
Field Shift turns NASA's view of the Earth

6
00:00:16,590 --> 00:00:18,890
into advice for one field.

7
00:00:19,050 --> 00:00:20,860
Here is how it works, on a pea field

8
00:00:20,910 --> 00:00:23,150
in the Huaral valley, in Peru.

9
00:00:24,550 --> 00:00:30,330
Start with your field. Use your GPS, search a place, or open the example site.

10
00:00:30,570 --> 00:00:33,370
Drop a point, or draw the outline.

11
00:00:33,830 --> 00:00:36,330
Field Shift measures the area for you.

12
00:00:38,370 --> 00:00:41,300
Then tell it what you would tell your agronomist.

13
00:00:41,350 --> 00:00:44,900
What grows now, what grew before, how you water.

14
00:00:44,950 --> 00:00:46,970
If you don't know, say so.

15
00:00:47,110 --> 00:00:50,540
Send photos at full resolution, or simply talk.

16
00:00:50,590 --> 00:00:54,810
It asks for what is missing, like a closer look at the underside of a leaf.

17
00:00:56,450 --> 00:00:59,590
Meanwhile, NASA data reads your field.

18
00:00:59,870 --> 00:01:02,420
40 years of NASA POWER weather show these weeks

19
00:01:02,470 --> 00:01:05,030
running 5 °C warmer than normal.

20
00:01:05,350 --> 00:01:08,150
NASA's SMAP satellite measures soil moisture.

21
00:01:08,450 --> 00:01:12,350
Sentinel-2 maps crop vigor, 10 m per pixel.

22
00:01:12,750 --> 00:01:15,040
Every reading shows its source, its date,

23
00:01:15,090 --> 00:01:18,210
and whether it describes your field or the whole region.

24
00:01:19,670 --> 00:01:22,910
From the temperature, degree-days count pest generations:

25
00:01:23,270 --> 00:01:25,930
aphids here complete about 3 more generations than normal.

26
00:01:27,550 --> 00:01:30,050
Then the readings become a plan.

27
00:01:30,470 --> 00:01:32,280
Prevention ranks the pests likely on your field,

28
00:01:32,330 --> 00:01:35,610
with NASA's GEOS-FP weather forecast.

29
00:01:35,750 --> 00:01:38,420
Organic care names the natural enemies to protect,

30
00:01:38,470 --> 00:01:41,180
like lady beetles and parasitoid wasps,

31
00:01:41,230 --> 00:01:44,230
and beneficial fungi such as Trichoderma.

32
00:01:44,670 --> 00:01:47,300
Rotation compares your current rotation with two alternatives,

33
00:01:47,350 --> 00:01:49,720
for soil health, water and pest cycles.

34
00:01:49,770 --> 00:01:53,040
And you can ask: what if I grow avocado?

35
00:01:53,090 --> 00:01:54,890
It is scored the same way.

36
00:01:56,950 --> 00:02:00,460
It all ends in a pre-diagnosis, not a diagnosis.

37
00:02:00,510 --> 00:02:03,760
Download the technical sheet, with every number cited,

38
00:02:03,810 --> 00:02:06,290
and confirm it with your agronomist.

39
00:02:09,050 --> 00:02:11,390
NASA watches the whole planet.

40
00:02:11,610 --> 00:02:13,990
Field Shift helps you read your own field.
